+<item>
+<title>Telegram macOS</title>
 <description>New:&lt;br&gt;• The Monochrome theme is now called Dictator: calmer contrast picked for readability, clear selected rows, a proper surface for suggestions above the input; it shows first in Appearance with a NEW badge until you try it&lt;br&gt;• The AI agent can change the app's whole look: any theme or accent color, chat backgrounds including a picture, the night theme, text size and bubbles, and it can design a theme of its own and share its link&lt;br&gt;• Widgets run faster on the updated Nova engine&lt;br&gt;• tg://companion and tg://agent open the Dictator setup&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Improved:&lt;br&gt;• The gift resale listings header now floats over the listings with a blurred, theme-shaded background, and its filter buttons are easier to read.&lt;br&gt;• Coming back to the AI Assistant reopens the chat you were writing in instead of a new one&lt;br&gt;• In AI chats the activity line glides with the reply instead of jumping&lt;br&gt;• A chat with its own theme colors the send, attach and other input buttons from that theme&lt;br&gt;• The gift marketplace is a little wider, its filters spread across the row, ribbon numbers stay white in every theme, and TON prices on cards show two decimals&lt;br&gt;• Less memory at launch: a faster scan of the media cache, a settings cache that really frees memory, and released database caches nobody reads&lt;br&gt;• Widgets and bot documents read HTML with a memory-safe parser, and helper services run with macOS Enhanced Security&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;• Scrolling gift resale listings no longer drops frames.&lt;br&gt;• The check in the verified badge stays readable with light custom accents&lt;br&gt;• Device icons in Active Sessions follow the Dictator theme&lt;br&gt;• Custom themes keep their own message bubble colors when applied again or shared&lt;br&gt;</description>
